01-genesis/25.tex-%	\footnote{
01-genesis/25.tex-%		Keturah. The most ignored significant person in the Torah. Rashi follows
01-genesis/25.tex-%		an old rabbinic idea that she is Hagar. But there is no basis for this
01-genesis/25.tex-%		in the text, and other traditional commentators reject it (Ibn Ezra,
01-genesis/25.tex-%		Ramban, Rashbam). Keturah is the mother of tribes located along the
01-genesis/25.tex-%		route of incense trade, and her name is related to the word for incense.
01-genesis/25.tex-%		Notably, the Midianites are among the children of Abraham and Keturah,
01-genesis/25.tex-%		and the influence of the Midianite priest Jethro on Moses, his
01-genesis/25.tex-%		son-in-law, is understood to be substantial. And the line of Levites who
01-genesis/25.tex-%		are descended from Moses thus—alone among the Israelites—derive from
01-genesis/25.tex-%		Abraham through both Sarah and Keturah.
01-genesis/25.tex-%	}
