01-genesis/25.tex-%		revelation, man is not more important than woman. The message is what is
01-genesis/25.tex-%		important. Rebekah hears first because her need arises first. She is
01-genesis/25.tex-%		troubled because of the struggling twins in her womb. Footnote 25:23.
01-genesis/25.tex-%		the older the younger will serve. As I explained in The Hidden Face of
01-genesis/25.tex-%		God, people have usually taken this to mean that YHWH tells Rebekah that
01-genesis/25.tex-%		her younger son, Jacob, will dominate her older one, Esau. Some have
01-genesis/25.tex-%		thought, therefore, that Rebekah is not really manipulating the
01-genesis/25.tex-%		succession when she sends Jacob to pose as Esau. Rather, she is simply
01-genesis/25.tex-%		fulfilling God’s will. The decision of who is number-one-son thus is
01-genesis/25.tex-%		still God’s. However, this understanding is based on a misunderstanding
01-genesis/25.tex-%		of the subtle, exquisitely ambiguous biblical wording. The text does not
01-genesis/25.tex-%		in fact say that the elder son will serve the younger son. In biblical
01-genesis/25.tex-%		Hebrew, the subject may either precede or follow the verb, and the
01-genesis/25.tex-%		object likewise may either precede or follow the verb. What that means
01-genesis/25.tex-%		is that sometimes it is impossible to tell which word in a biblical
01-genesis/25.tex-%		verse is the subject and which is the object, especially if the verse is
