01-genesis/32.tex-	Nobody knows what's going on in this line or why it's here.%
01-genesis/32.tex-	\fC{
01-genesis/32.tex-		There are some remarkable Semitic comparanda for the sound sequence
01-genesis/32.tex-		\textit{r-ʾ-l}. Classical Arabic \textit{raʾl} means a young ostrich,
01-genesis/32.tex-		with associated imagery of rapid, frightened or wild movement, and
01-genesis/32.tex-		\textit{Rʾl} is independently attested as a personal name in ancient
01-genesis/32.tex-		Safaitic. Most strikingly, Ibn Manzur preserves an old poem in which a
01-genesis/32.tex-		woman propositions a man and touches his penis; in the immediately
01-genesis/32.tex-		following line the speaker describes what happens to his \textit{raʾl},
01-genesis/32.tex-		which the lexicographer explains through the behavior of the young
01-genesis/32.tex-		ostrich. Thus \textit{raʾl} does not lexically mean ``penis,'' but an
01-genesis/32.tex-		explicitly penile metaphor using the word is independently attested.
01-genesis/32.tex-		A neighboring but phonologically distinct Arabic root,
01-genesis/32.tex-		\textit{r-ʿ-l}, means to stab, pierce, or thrust violently, while
01-genesis/32.tex-		Aramaic \textit{r-ʿ-l} means ``tremble.'' Farther north, the obscure
01-genesis/32.tex-		form \textit{ʾ-r-ʾ-l} occurs in Hebrew and, remarkably, in the Moabite
01-genesis/32.tex-		Mesha inscription in connection with Israel; its meaning is disputed,
01-genesis/32.tex-		with proposals ranging from a cultic object to a human leader.
01-genesis/32.tex-		No corresponding anatomical \textit{r-ʾ-l} has been securely found in
01-genesis/32.tex-		Ugaritic or Akkadian. None of this establishes an etymology for
01-genesis/32.tex-		\textit{Israel}---whose apparent final \textit{r-ʾ-l} crosses the
01-genesis/32.tex-		ordinary morpheme boundary before \textit{El}---but it supplies an
01-genesis/32.tex-		unusually rich set of ancient sound-associations for possible
01-genesis/32.tex-		paronomasia, including, rather inconveniently, an independently
01-genesis/32.tex-		attested sexual one.
01-genesis/32.tex-	}
