08-samuel/1-17.tex-\Verse{26}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	\hX{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		וַיֹּאמֶר דָּוִד אֶל־הָאֲנָשִׁים הָעֹמְדִים עִמּוֹ לֵאמֹר מַה־יֵּעָשֶׂה לָאִישׁ אֲשֶׁר יַכֶּה אֶת־הַפְּלִשְׁתִּי הַלָּז וְהֵסִיר חֶרְפָּה מֵעַל יִשְׂרָאֵל כִּי מִי הַפְּלִשְׁתִּי
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		הֶעָרֵל הַזֶּה כִּי חֵרֵף מַעַרְכוֹת אֱלֹהִים חַיִּים׃
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	\eX{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		David asked the men standing near him, “What will be done for the
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		man who kills that Philistine and removes the disgrace from
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		Israel? Who is that uncircumcised Philistine that he dares defy
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		the ranks of the living God?”
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	\aB{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		David's like ``Say that again, I was watching the sheep earlier.''
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	\aB{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		Then he calls him a foreskin.
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	\aC{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		The Hebrew \heb{הערלהזה} can be parsed as:
08-samuel/1-17.tex-
08-samuel/1-17.tex:		\Table{ll}{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-			\heb{ה + ערל + הזה}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-				& ``this uncircumcised one'' \\
08-samuel/1-17.tex-			\heb{ה + ערלה + זה}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-				& ``this foreskin''
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		The latter's a bit grammatically off, since it's the masculine word for ``this'' while foreskin is feminine.
08-samuel/1-17.tex-
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		Then again, the only grammatical sin you have to commit to make it work is to treat the word ``foreskin'' as masculine and not feminine, which isn't exactly a stretch for a sufficiently playful (read: awake) author, given that foreskins are, well. Nevermind. Forget I said anything.
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-
08-samuel/1-17.tex-\Verse{27}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	\hX{וַיֹּאמֶר לוֹ הָעָם כַּדָּבָר הַזֶּה לֵאמֹר כֹּה יֵעָשֶׂה לָאִישׁ אֲשֶׁר יַכֶּנּוּ׃}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	\eX{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		The troops told him in the same words what would be done for the
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		man who killed him.
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	\aB{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		So the troops update David on the payoff structure of the situation.
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-
08-samuel/1-17.tex-\Verse{28}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	\hX{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלִיאָב אָחִיו הַגָּדוֹל בְּדַבְּרוֹ אֶל־הָאֲנָשִׁים וַיִּחַר־אַף אֱלִיאָב בְּדָוִד וַיֹּאמֶר לָמָּה־זֶּה יָרַדְתָּ וְעַל־מִי נָטַשְׁתָּ מְעַט הַצֹּאן הָהֵנָּה
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		בַּמִּדְבָּר אֲנִי יָדַעְתִּי אֶת־זְדֹנְךָ וְאֵת רֹעַ לְבָבֶךָ כִּי לְמַעַן רְאוֹת הַמִּלְחָמָה יָרָדְתָּ׃
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	\eX{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		When Eliab, his oldest brother, heard him speaking to the men,
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		Eliab became angry with David and said, “Why did you come down
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		here, and with whom did you leave those few sheep in the
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		wilderness? I know your impudence and your impertinence: you came
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		down to watch the fighting!”
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	\aB{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		Now older brother is like ``Why are you here? Who's watching the sheep? You disrespectful little... You just wanted to watch the fight!''
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-
08-samuel/1-17.tex-\Verse{29}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	\hX{וַיֹּאמֶר דָּוִד מֶה עָשִׂיתִי עָתָּה הֲלוֹא דָּבָר הוּא׃}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	\eX{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		But David replied, “What have I done now? I was only asking!”
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	\aB{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		And David's like Jesus.
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	\aB{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		No need to get all mad.
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-
08-samuel/1-17.tex-\Verse{30}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	\hX{וַיִּסֹּב מֵאֶצְלוֹ אֶל־מוּל אַחֵר וַיֹּאמֶר כַּדָּבָר הַזֶּה וַיְשִׁבֻהוּ הָעָם דָּבָר כַּדָּבָר הָרִאשׁוֹן׃}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	\eX{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		And he turned away from him toward someone else; he asked the same
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		question, and the troops gave him the same answer as before.
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	\aB{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		So he asks someone else and they say the same thing.
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-
08-samuel/1-17.tex-\Verse{31}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	\hX{וַיִּשָּׁמְעוּ הַדְּבָרִים אֲשֶׁר דִּבֶּר דָּוִד וַיַּגִּדוּ לִפְנֵי־שָׁאוּל וַיִּקָּחֵהוּ׃}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	\eX{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		The things David said were overheard and were reported to Saul,
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		who had him brought over.
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	\aB{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		Saul hears all the things David's been saying (which things?) and has him brought over.
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-}
--
08-samuel/1-17.tex-}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	\aA{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		In summary, David wins.
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	\aA{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		The text notes he had no sword.
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-
08-samuel/1-17.tex-\Verse{51}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	\hX{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		וַיָּרץ דָּוִד וַיַּעֲמֹד אֶל־הַפְּלִשְׁתִּי וַיִּקַּח אֶת־חַרְבּוֹ וַיִּשְׁלְפָהּ מִתַּעְרָהּ וַיְמֹתְתֵהוּ וַיִּכְרת־בָּהּ אֶת־רֹאשׁוֹ וַיִּרְאוּ הַפְּלִשְׁתִּים כִּי־מֵת
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		גִּבּוֹרָם וַיָּנֻסוּ׃
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	\eX{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		so David ran up and stood over the Philistine, grasped his sword
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		and pulled it from its sheath; and with it he dispatched him and
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		cut off his head. When the Philistines saw that their warrior was
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		dead, they ran.
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	\aB{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		So he takes out his sword.
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	\aB{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		And cuts off his head.
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	\aB{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		And the other team decides to head home early today.
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-
08-samuel/1-17.tex-\Verse{52}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	\hX{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		וַיָּקֻמוּ אַנְשֵׁי יִשְׂרָאֵל וִיהוּדָה וַיָּרִעוּ וַיִּרְדְּפוּ אֶת־הַפְּלִשְׁתִּים עַד־בּוֹאֲךָ גַיְא וְעַד שַׁעֲרֵי עֶקְרוֹן וַיִּפְּלוּ חַלְלֵי פְלִשְׁתִּים בְּדֶרֶךְ
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		שַׁעֲרַיִם וְעַד־גַּת וְעַד־עֶקְרוֹן׃
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	\eX{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		The men of Israel and Judah rose up with a war cry and they
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		pursued the Philistines all the way to Gai and up to the gates of
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		Ekron; the Philistines fell mortally wounded along the road to
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		Shaarim up to Gath and Ekron.
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	}
