08-samuel/1-17.tex-	}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	\aB{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		David takes the head to Jerusalem which is sort of a minor plot hole.\footnote{Jerusalem isn't conquered until 2 Samuel 5. Judges 1:21 says the Jebusites were still living there with Benjamin. David has no meaningful connection with Jerusalem before he captures it. Rather, David is associated with Bethlehem (his birthplace), Judah and Hebron (where he reigns for 7½ years), the wilderness (Adullam, Ziph, En-gedi), and Ziklag (given to him by Achish) but Jerusalem is essentially absent from David's story until the conquest.}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	}
08-samuel/1-17.tex-
08-samuel/1-17.tex-	\aB{
08-samuel/1-17.tex-		And he also takes his weapons to his tent.
